WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.230
We're going to try to hack our own agents

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:03.560
by ourselves.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.080
I'm going to make the agent to send money

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.040
to an attacker.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.580
And then we'll see how our smart contract

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.560
handles it.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.200
So now the question is, what happens if

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:19.880
you have a bug in your program

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.480
or your bot has a bug, or there's an

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.320
injection, maybe prompt injection,

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.590
and then it drains everything you have

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.000
inside your wallet?

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.070
So I give my agent a budget that's at

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.800
most 0.1 per payment

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.640
and then 0.5 per day.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.150
So only this can be able to be used to

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.960
shop and then in the experience in 70s.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.190
So now this limits live in the smart

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.800
contract, not in the website

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:49.800
and not in the AI.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.410
So if the agent is hacked now, it does

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:55.000
not affect it.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.610
So this actually functions based on the

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.520
SpendShield tools only.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:03.110
And so now the agent holds no money and

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:03.840
no gas.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.660
So it only signs and then relates the

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:10.600
same, the reliance and the transaction.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:13.320
So they're going to try to hack that real

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:13.800
agent.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.520
And then we're going to put it in, that's

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:17.600
in red-team mode.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.630
We're going to tell the agent to be

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:20.800
anything it reads.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.720
So we can see the amount.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.420
The agent is trying to send to the

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.280
attacker here.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.080
So now it has been blocked.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.560
As you can see, it has been blocked by

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:34.920
SpendShield here.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.440
It has blocked the transaction.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.080
It has tried again for the second time

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.600
and the transaction was also blocked here,

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.520
if you notice.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:47.760
So now I've received a message here

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.440
telling me to review requests

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.280
from the bot.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:55.420
So even when it's been hacked, we are

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.680
able to reject so nobody can be able to

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:58.760
spend directly

00:01:58.760 --> 00:01:59.760
from the bot.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.990
So you can see that the transaction field

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:03.920
here on the blockchain explorer.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.260
So it means that's actually been blocked

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.400
accurately the way we want it now.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.000
So if everything ever goes wrong, one

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.160
click freezes every agent.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:13.390
So we're going to go back to three school

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:14.360
agents here.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:20.360
So that's like the kill switch.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.960
So now the agent tries to buy something

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.240
and then it refused instant.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.080
The owner froze all agents spending.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.310
So one more thing, QDay is moving to

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.480
post-quantum safety.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.980
So even if someone breaks an agent's key

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.320
one day, they can only spend 50 cents a

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:33.720
day.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.080
And I can stop them with my phone.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.070
So shops that sell data to agents like

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:42.150
the one in my demo piece was just small

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:42.960
fee pass

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:43.960
here.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.520
A company's running many agents give each

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.720
one its own budget and gets alerts.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.330
So basically you can give your agents a

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.680
budget not your wallet.

